    "id": "p10-q16-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "16",
    "prompt": "$ABCD$ is a rectangle. Equilateral triangles $ABX$ and $DAY$ are drawn outside $ABCD$. Draw a diagram and prove that triangle $CXY$ is equilateral.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$CX=CY=XY$, so $\\triangle CXY$ is equilateral.",
      "worked": "The equilateral triangles give $XB=XA=AB$ and $DY=AY=AD$. The rectangle gives $AB=CD$ and $AD=BC$. Thus each of triangles XBC, CDY and XAY has one included side of length AB and one of length AD. Also $\\angle XBC=90^\\circ+60^\\circ=150^\\circ$, $\\angle CDY=90^\\circ+60^\\circ=150^\\circ$, and $\\angle XAY=360^\\circ-(60^\\circ+90^\\circ+60^\\circ)=150^\\circ$. Therefore $\\triangle XBC\\cong\\triangle CDY\\cong\\triangle XAY$ by SAS. The sides opposite the equal150-degree angles correspond, so $XC=CY=XY$. Hence triangle CXY is equilateral.",
